# Provider binaries, 700 MB of them, and the lock that names their hashes per
# platform. The lock is normally committed. It is not here because nothing has been
# applied, so pinning hashes resolved on one throwaway Linux container would be
# claiming a reproducibility this directory does not have yet. It gets committed on
# the first run that produces a plan.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl

# State, and the variable file holding the project id. Neither should ever be here.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
